/* book exam traps: Using α = 1/(2RC) in a series RLC circuit; the series value is R/(2L). | Squaring only one side. Compare α with ω₀ (the easy test), or α² with ω₀², but never α² with ω₀. α = 12 s⁻¹ with ω₀ = 10 rad/s is overdamped: 12 > 10 and 144 > 100. | Letting vC or iL jump at the switch; both are continuous, and their 0⁻ values set the constants. | Writing ωd = √(α² − ω₀²); for underdamped it is √(ω₀² − α²), a real positive number. */
