/* book: lead: Two numbers describe every second-order circuit. The natural frequency ωn (rad/s) says how fast the circuit would oscillate with no energy loss. The damping ratio ζ (no unit) says how strongly resistance kills that oscillation. From them you get the pole positions, the ringing frequency, the overshoot, the peak time and the settling time. Designers use this language for filters, speaker crossovers */
