/* book Worked example: Q: A series RLC circuit has R = 20 Ω, L = 0.1 H and C = 10 μF. A 10 V step is applied at t = 0 with zero initial energy. Find ωn, α, ζ, ωd, percentage overshoot, peak time and 2 % settling time.
   1. Compute LC = (0.1 H)(10 × 10⁻⁶ F) = 1 × 10⁻⁶ s². Then ωn = 1/√(LC) = 1/√(1 × 10⁻⁶) = 1000 rad/s.
   2. For a series RLC, α = R/(2L) = 20 Ω/(2 × 0.1 H) = 100 s⁻¹.
   3. ζ = α/ωn = 100/1000 = 0.1. The circuit is underdamped.
   4. √(1 − ζ²) = √(1 − 0.01) = √0.99 = 0.994987. ωd = 1000 × 0.994987 = 994.987 rad/s ≈ 995 rad/s.
   5. Exponent = πζ/√(1 − ζ²) = (3.14159 × 0.1)/0.994987 = 0.315741. e−0.315741 = 0.7293. Overshoot = 100 × 0.7293 = 72.93 % ≈ 72.9 %.
   6. tp = π/ωd = 3.14159/994.987 = 0.003157 s = 3.157 ms ≈ 3.16 ms.
   7. ts ≈ 4/(ζωn) = 4/(0.1 × 1000) = 4/100 = 0.04 s = 40 ms.
   Answer: ωn = 1000 rad/s, α = 100 s⁻¹, ζ = 0.1, ωd ≈ 995 rad/s, overshoot ≈ 72.9 %, tp ≈ 3.16 ms and ts ≈ 40 ms. */
